  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe probe for #1551 shows that the corner slivers are true rest material. It is not a sim gap and not a carry gap. This PR adds no product code. It adds a pinning suite and a decision file.\n\n- `EM-0600-4FL` is a 6 mm end mill, not a 0.6 in end mill.\n- The contour runs on the part offset at r = 3 mm with round corners. It sweeps every point within 6 mm of a part corner.\n- The stock corner is 7.07 mm from the part corner. Thus a sliver stays at each stock corner (legs 1.68 mm, area 1.227 mm^2).\n- The carried body keeps 40 full-height brim columns (10 at each corner), all 6.02 mm to 6.81 mm from the part corner. No full-height column is inside the swept disc.\n\nThe probe result is on the issue. The decision is in `docs/decisions/1551-corner-sliver-true-rest.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/carried_corner_rest.rs`:\n\n- `a_6mm_contour_leaves_the_true_corner_sliver_and_nothing_else`: no full-height column inside the swept disc (false rest), no cut column outside it (lost material), and the sliver area agrees with the analytic area.\n- `an_8mm_contour_cuts_the_stock_corners_through`: with `EM-0800-4FL` (reach 8 mm), no full-height brim column stays.\n\nRed check: the 8 mm assertions, run on the 6 mm tool as a temporary edit, fail with the 40 corner columns. The suite passes on main without a code change, because there is no defect.\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` is green (1 step, `app:carried_corner_rest`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test carried_corner_rest -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The in-setup stock sim of Setup1 (not carried) was not compared column by column. The carried body is the body the fixture check reads.\n- The field engine (#637) was not run. The suite uses the default column body.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1551\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
